From: MacSW maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Serialize macOS process write-buffer barriers.

Concurrent NtFlushProcessWriteBuffers callers can hang in
thread_get_register_pointer_values / thread_get_state under Rosetta. A
standalone eight-thread probe reproduces the hang without SOLIDWORKS.

Serialize the register-query loop, retaining the barrier for every thread
and all Mach resource cleanup. Do not replace the process-wide barrier
with a local fence or a no-op. Linux and other platform paths are unchanged.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -7055,6 +7055,7 @@
 NTSTATUS WINAPI NtFlushProcessWriteBuffers(void)
 {
     /* Taken from https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/7be37908e5a1cbb83b1062768c1649827eeaceaa/src/coreclr/pal/src/thread/process.cpp#L2799 */
+    static pthread_mutex_t flush_mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
     mach_msg_type_number_t count, i;
     thread_act_array_t threads;
 
@@ -7064,6 +7065,9 @@
     /* Get references to all threads of this process */
     if (task_threads( mach_task_self(), &threads, &count )) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 
+    /* Concurrent register queries can deadlock under Rosetta. Keep the
+     * process-wide barrier, but let only one caller enumerate registers. */
+    pthread_mutex_lock( &flush_mutex );
     for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
     {
         uintptr_t reg_values[128];
@@ -7074,6 +7078,7 @@
         p_thread_get_register_pointer_values( threads[i], &sp, &reg_count, reg_values );
         mach_port_deallocate( mach_task_self(), threads[i] );
     }
+    pthread_mutex_unlock( &flush_mutex );
     vm_deallocate( mach_task_self(), (vm_address_t)threads, count * sizeof(threads[0]) );
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
